    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d419-a3">

                <pb facs="0785" n="675" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg675"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 472.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pratt to Colonel
                            Stewart.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-07-05"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 5,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am now in receipt of your dispatch of the
                    28th ultimo, from which I note that you have received my Nos. 3 and 4 and that
                    all the witnesses subpoenaed by you to testify for the prosecution at the trial
                    of the assassin Minas had arrived, except the woman Asli, whom you had found it
                    necessary to summon through the. Persian authorities.</p>
                <p>Under the circumstances, I agree with you that it was best not to insist upon Mr.
                    Wright’s appearing at the trial if his testimony could be dispensed with.</p>
                <p>The charges in the list which you inclose appear to fully cover the case, besides
                    having the advantage of being both concise and to the point.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Spencer Pratt</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
